# Nissan Note E11 five-door hatchback, 2006-2012.
#
# The first Note: a tall mini-MPV hatchback with a high roofline and a short blunt
# nose, sold in Britain from 2006. The European-market pre-facelift car is
# modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Note
#
# Dimensions 4.080 x 1.690 x 1.550 m, wheelbase 2.600 m, from the English
# Wikipedia E11 dimension box.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the E11 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names: white, silver, blue and red. Weights white 3, silver 3, blue 2,
# red 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 165 km/h for the 1.4, the volume UK engine. Comfort 85/310, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 85, the same as the Juke F15: roomy for its size but short-legged.
# Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: May 2006 intro, retires staggered 2021-2024 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-note-e11.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-note-e11.dae (45 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-note-e11/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons; the pack
# mixes Japanese and European cars, and the European pre-facelift nose is the one
# modelled).
#
# Recorded limitation: no strict side profile exists, so the proportions are
# dimension-calibrated and the contours taken from oblique photographs.
# Accepted deviations: the body and rear corners are more angular than the
# photographs. At 128 px the tall cabin, the upright hatch and the high corner
# lamps read as the Note.

obj=citycar
name=NissanNoteE11(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2006
intro_month=5
retire_year=2024
retire_month=6
speed=165
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=85
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=310

